    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="10" relname="span">I thin[k] learnability is a signficant part of usabiltiy.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="3" relname="volitional-cause">You will find that the eaiser a user can logicaly manouver through an application,</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="11" relname="span">the more comfortable they will be.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="5" relname="volitional-cause">If a product is easy to learn and not riddled with errors</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="12" relname="span">you'll find that the IT staff will receive less support class from users to fix a bug or explain a process.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="13" relname="span">I believe that users must be the experts in their line of busniess applications.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="6" relname="volitional-cause">How good they are at using the application and understanding it will ultimately dictate the overall usabiltiy of the product</segment>
